{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"double","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDouble","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDoubleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"double","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLTransposeV7ContentV6doubleAA9MXLDoubleVSgvp","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct\/double"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct\/double"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"double","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDouble","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDoubleV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDouble"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<double>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"If the double element is present, it indicates that the music is doubled one octave from what is currently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose/Content-swift.struct/double":{"abstract":[{"text":"If the double element is present, it indicates that the music is doubled one octave from what is currently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written.","type":"text"}],"title":"double","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct\/double","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"double","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDoubleV","text":"MXLDouble","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct\/double"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose/Content-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transpose group represents what must be added to a written pitch to get a correct sounding pitch."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTranspose.Content","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transpose type represents what must be added to a written pitch to get a correct sounding pitch. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional number attribute refers to staff numbers, from top to bottom on the system. If absent, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transposition applies to all staves in the part. Per-staff transposition is most often used in parts that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent multiple instruments."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTranspose","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTranspose","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTranspose","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDouble":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The double type indicates that the music is doubled one octave from what is currently written. If the above","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to yes, the doubling is one octave above what is written, as for mixed flute \/ piccolo parts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in band literature. Otherwise the doubling is one octave below what is written, as for mixed cello \/ bass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parts in orchestral literature.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldouble","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDouble"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLDouble","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDouble"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDouble","role":"symbol"}}}